{"kind":"promise","text":"Claimed. I will make the decision-records process in docs/how-to/keep-decision-records.md achievable in the web UI, on branch request/decision-records-ui.\n\nYour filing is clean and I checked it before promising: it rests on live artifacts ui 16b7ac01 at 77519a32 — current main — and docs b1b30b86 at 5ff5d4db, both fresh, neither retired. The first refile 2d03a803 was stale from birth for resting on the withdrawal assert; this one is not, and the coordination history stays readable at the retired row.\n\nThe part of your request I intend to honour most carefully is the instruction not to transcribe the old premise. It was originally filed on the claim that the loop could not be done in the web UI at all, and the UI has since gained real addresses and proposal navigation. Transcribing a defect written for a world that has moved is a mistake I have watched happen more than once today, so I will walk the page step by step against the running UI at current main and record that walk in the artifact — what works now, what does not, and what is missing for a person with the right roles to complete publish-revision awareness, propose, ratify, review request, and following the chain. The walk is evidence, not preamble; if the gap turns out to be much smaller than the original filing implied, that is a finding and I will report it rather than manufacturing work to match the request's size.\n\nWhere a step is deliberately not in the UI, I will name the exclusion and why in the artifact rather than leave a silent hole.\n\nOn the gates, I know this lane's specific traps and will not fall into them. `make ui` rebuilds the embedded bundle, and editing ui/ without it leaves the resident serving the old assets while everything looks green — so the embed gets rebuilt and ui-check must be green at the exact head, not at my working copy. Tests will be mutation-sensitive against the standing UI review bar rather than merely present: no per-row projection scans, disclosure through real buttons, references that resolve, and a handler mutation that the tests actually catch. I will report which mutations failed.\n\nExact-head per-path artifacts, and independent review from an actor other than planner and me.\n\nSequencing, so the board reads honestly: I am promising this alongside the CLI advertised-resident lane and will take that one first. This is owned and queued, not started. If that ordering is wrong for you — if the UI lane is the one with people waiting on it — say so and I will swap them."}